2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8753acb88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 33019, \"chunk_count\": 21, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:16\", \"token_count\": 10517, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"  These fixes were accepted because data races are bugs, not \\\"concurrency mechanisms left to users.\\\"\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-07]\\n\\n# Pull Request: otelgin: remove unneeded context save/restore to avoid data race (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#8014)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/8014  \\n\\n**Author**: nicksherron  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-10-14T04:01:24Z · **Updated**: 2025-10-17T10:42:07Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: closed  \\n\\n**Branch**: `fix/otelgin-data-race` → `main`  \\n\\n**Changes**: +83 / -10 across 2 files  \\n\\n**Labels**: —  \\n\\n**Milestone**: —\\n\\n---\\n\\n## The Race Is Real and Reproducible\\n\\n  From issue #4588:\\n\\n  WARNING: DATA RACE\\n\\n  Write at 0x... by goroutine X:\\n\\n    [defer in Middleware]\\n\\n  Read at 0x... by goroutine Y:\\n\\n    [user handler accessing context]\\n\\n  This is undefined behavior. The Go memory model states: \\\"Programs that modify data being simultaneously accessed by multiple goroutines must serialize such access.\\\"\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-07]\\n\\n# Pull Request: otelgin: remove unneeded context save/restore to avoid data race (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#8014)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/8014  \\n\\n**Author**: nicksherron  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-10-14T04:01:24Z · **Updated**: 2025-10-17T10:42:07Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: closed  \\n\\n**Branch**: `fix/otelgin-data-race` → `main`  \\n\\n**Changes**: +83 / -10 across 2 files  \\n\\n**Labels**: —  \\n\\n**Milestone**: —\\n\\n---\\n\\n## The Fix is Correct\\n\\n  The fix simply removes dead code:\\n\\n```go\\n\\n  // Before: Save and restore (unnecessary)\\n\\n  savedCtx := c.Request.Context()\\n\\n  defer func() { c.Request = c.Request.WithContext(savedCtx) }()\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"these fix were accept becaus data race are bug not concurr mechan left to user sourc id src pr 07 pull request otelgin remov unneed context save restor to avoid data race open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 8014 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 8014 author nicksherron creat 2025 10 14t04 01 24z updat 2025 10 17t10 42 07z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state close branch fix otelgin data race main chang 83 10 across 2 file label mileston the race is real and reproduc from issu 4588 warn data race write at 0x by goroutin x defer in middlewar read at 0x by goroutin y user handler access context this is undefin behavior the go memori model state program that modifi data be simultan access by multipl goroutin must serial such access sourc id src pr 07 pull request otelgin remov unneed context save restor to avoid data race open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 8014 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 8014 author nicksherron creat 2025 10 14t04 01 24z updat 2025 10 17t10 42 07z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state close branch fix otelgin data race main chang 83 10 across 2 file label mileston the fix is correct the fix simpli remov dead code go befor save and restor unnecessari savedctx c request context defer func c request c request withcontext savedctx\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8753acb88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"id\": \"b40b58fd0d2fea42\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3203583323344643, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.153940263334949, \"vector_similarity\": 0.70866716, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8753acb88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 33019, \"chunk_count\": 21, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:16\", \"token_count\": 10517, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"=====================================\\n\\n+ Hits       11598   11605    +7     \\n\\n+ Misses      2808    2795   -13     \\n\\n  Partials     354     354           \\n\\n```\\n\\n... and [1 file with indirect coverage changes](https://app.codecov.io/gh/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/8014/indirect-changes?src=pr&el=tree-more&utm_medium=referral&utm_source=github&utm_content=comment&utm_campaign=pr+comments&utm_term=open-telemetry)\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary> :rocket: New features to boost your workflow: </summary>\\n\\n- :snowflake: [Test Analytics](https://docs.codecov.com/docs/test-analytics): Detect flaky tests, report on failures, and find test suite problems.\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n---\\n\\n**dmathieu** — 2025-10-14T07:54:22Z\\n\\nThe intent of the defer is to remove the span from the context, so spans using the same context aren't childs of the created span once the middleware has finished running.\\n\\nImaging the following setup:\\n\\n```golang\\n\\nr := gin.New()\\n\\nr.Use(myCustomMiddleware)\\n\\nr.Use(otelgin.Middleware(\\\"my-server\\\"))\\n\\nr.GET(\\\"/\\\", func(c *gin.Context) {\\n\\n\\tc.HTML(http.StatusOK, \\\"index.tmpl\\\", gin.H{})\\n\\n})\\n\\n```\\n\\nWhen `myCustomMiddleware` runs, the span has either not started yet, or is already finished.\\n\\nIf it's already finished, the context shouldn't have the span within it, as we're not within the trace anymore.\\n\\nRight now, if you create a span within `myCustomMiddleware`, after the call to `c.Next()`, it won't be a child of the otelgin span.\\n\\nAfter your change it is one.\\n\\nThis is what the defer prevents.\\n\\nWhile I agree to fixing this race condition, the defer does have a use and I don't think we can just drop it.\\n\\n(ideally, we should add a test for this too)\\n\\n---\\n\\n**akats7** — 2025-10-14T08:01:45Z\\n\\n> The intent of the defer is to remove the span from the context, so spans using the same context aren't childs of the created span once the middleware has finished running.\\n\\n> \\n\\n> Imaging the following setup:\\n\\n> \\n\\n> ```go\\n\\n> r := gin.New()\\n\\n> r.Use(myCustomMiddleware)\\n\\n> r.Use(otelgin.Middleware(\\\"my-server\\\"))\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"hit 11598 11605 7 miss 2808 2795 13 partial 354 354 and 1 file with indirect coverag chang http app codecov io gh open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 8014 indirect chang src pr el tree more utm _ medium referr utm _ sourc github utm _ content comment utm _ campaign pr comment utm _ term open telemetri detail detail summari rocket new featur to boost your workflow summari snowflak test analyt http doc codecov com doc test analyt detect flaki test report on failur and find test suit problem detail dmathieu 2025 10 14t07 54 22z the intent of the defer is to remov the span from the context so span use the same context aren t child of the creat span onc the middlewar ha finish run imag the follow setup golang r gin new r use mycustommiddlewar r use otelgin middlewar my server r get func c gin context c html http statusok index tmpl gin h when mycustommiddlewar run the span ha either not start yet or is alreadi finish if it s alreadi finish the context shouldn t have the span within it a we re not within the trace anymor right now if you creat a span within mycustommiddlewar after the call to c next it won t be a child of the otelgin span after your chang it is one this is what the defer prevent while i agre to fix this race condit the defer doe have a use and i don t think we can just drop it ideal we should add a test for this too akats7 2025 10 14t08 01 45z the intent of the defer is to remov the span from the context so span use the same context aren t child of the creat span onc the middlewar ha finish run imag the follow setup go r gin new r use mycustommiddlewar r use otelgin middlewar my server\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8753acb88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"id\": \"dfdecac4ba6df693\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3195961193344643, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.15394026333494906, \"vector_similarity\": 0.70612645, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8753acb88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 33019, \"chunk_count\": 21, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:16\", \"token_count\": 10517, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"https://gist.github.com/nicksherron/08dfbc599e0de0532cd4dc0d30f9f4a4 (moved to a gist to save the thread from a giant comment)\\n\\nBy the way I'm really blown away by your quick responses. I never see this kind of quick back and forth on a new PR in other oss projects. I'm really impressed and it's much appreciated. \\n\\n---\\n\\n**nicksherron** — 2025-10-14T05:23:38Z\\n\\nI can also provide a benchmark to prove the performance impact is actually net positive if you'd like @flc1125 \\n\\n---\\n\\n**flc1125** — 2025-10-14T06:05:25Z\\n\\n> https://gist.github.com/nicksherron/08dfbc599e0de0532cd4dc0d30f9f4a4\\n\\n<details>\\n\\n<summary>This is a minimal case to examine the issue of data races:</summary>\\n\\n```go\\n\\npackage otelgin\\n\\nimport (\\n\\n\\t\\\"context\\\"\\n\\n\\t\\\"net/http/httptest\\\"\\n\\n\\t\\\"sync\\\"\\n\\n\\t\\\"testing\\\"\\n\\n\\t\\\"github.com/gin-gonic/gin\\\"\\n\\n\\t\\\"github.com/stretchr/testify/assert\\\"\\n\\n)\\n\\nfunc TestConcurrency(t *testing.T) {\\n\\n\\tt.Run(\\\"no defer\\\", func(t *testing.T) {\\n\\n\\t\\trunConcurrency(t, noDeferMiddleware())\\n\\n\\t})\\n\\n\\tt.Run(\\\"have defer\\\", func(t *testing.T) {\\n\\n\\t\\trunConcurrency(t, haveDeferMiddleware())\\n\\n\\t})\\n\\n\\tt.Run(\\\"no middleware\\\", func(t *testing.T) {\\n\\n\\t\\trunConcurrency(t, nil)\\n\\n\\t})\\n\\n}\\n\\nfunc runConcurrency(t *testing.T, middleware gin.HandlerFunc) {\\n\\n\\trouter := gin.New()\\n\\n\\tif middleware != nil {\\n\\n\\t\\trouter.Use(middleware)\\n\\n\\t}\\n\\n\\trouter.POST(\\\"/test\\\", func(c *gin.Context) {\\n\\n\\t\\tgo func() {\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t_ = c.Request.Context()\\n\\n\\t\\t}()\\n\\n\\t\\tc.String(200, \\\"ok\\\")\\n\\n\\t})\\n\\n\\twg := sync.WaitGroup{}\\n\\n\\tfor i := 0; i < 1000; i++ {\\n\\n\\t\\twg.Go(func() {\\n\\n\\t\\t\\treq := httptest.NewRequest(\\\"POST\\\", \\\"/test\\\", nil)\\n\\n\\t\\t\\tw := httptest.NewRecorder()\\n\\n\\t\\t\\trouter.ServeHTTP(w, req)\\n\\n\\t\\t\\tassert.Equal(t, 200, w.Code)\\n\\n\\t\\t})\\n\\n\\t}\\n\\n\\twg.Wait()\\n\\n}\\n\\nfunc noDeferMiddleware() gin.HandlerFunc {\\n\\n\\treturn func(c *gin.Context) {\\n\\n\\t\\tc.Request.WithContext(\\n\\n\\t\\t\\tcontext.WithValue(c.Request.Context(), \\\"key1\\\", \\\"value1\\\"),\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"http gist github com nicksherron 08dfbc599e0de0532cd4dc0d30f9f4a4 move to a gist to save the thread from a giant comment by the way i m realli blown away by your quick respons i never see this kind of quick back and forth on a new pr in other os project i m realli impress and it s much appreci nicksherron 2025 10 14t05 23 38z i can also provid a benchmark to prove the perform impact is actual net posit if you d like flc1125 flc1125 2025 10 14t06 05 25z http gist github com nicksherron 08dfbc599e0de0532cd4dc0d30f9f4a4 detail summari this is a minim case to examin the issu of data race summari go packag otelgin import context net http httptest sync test github com gin gonic gin github com stretchr testifi assert func testconcurr t test t t run no defer func t test t runconcurr t nodefermiddlewar t run have defer func t test t runconcurr t havedefermiddlewar t run no middlewar func t test t runconcurr t nil func runconcurr t test t middlewar gin handlerfunc router gin new if middlewar nil router use middlewar router post test func c gin context go func _ c request context c string 200 ok wg sync waitgroup for i 0 i 1000 i wg go func req httptest newrequest post test nil w httptest newrecord router servehttp w req assert equal t 200 w code wg wait func nodefermiddlewar gin handlerfunc return func c gin context c request withcontext context withvalu c request context key1 value1\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8753acb88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"id\": \"31ad922bbde87a9e\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id