o fix this race condit the defer doe have a use and i don t think we can just drop it ideal we should add a test for this too akats7 2025 10 14t08 01 45z the intent of the defer is to remov the span from the context so span use the same context aren t child of the creat span onc the middlewar ha finish run imag the follow setup go r gin new r use mycustommiddlewar r use otelgin middlewar my server\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8753acb88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"id\": \"dfdecac4ba6df693\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.40972960692199895, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.31008949560285565, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6422232, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8753acb88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 33019, \"chunk_count\": 21, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:16\", \"token_count\": 10517, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"> \\\"Contexts form a tree... Successive calls to WithValue, WithCancel, WithDeadline, or WithTimeout derive new contexts.\\\"\\n\\nContexts are meant to flow forward, not be \\\"restored\\\" backward. The library shouldn't enforce this opinion.\\n\\n2. Most users want otelgin early in the chain\\n\\nI (and I assume most users) place otelgin as one of the first middleware specifically so child spans can be created from it:\\n\\nr.Use(otelgin.Middleware(\\\"my-service\\\"))  // ← First - creates root span\\n\\nr.Use(loggingMiddleware)                  // ← Creates child spans\\n\\nr.Use(authMiddleware)                     // ← Creates child spans\\n\\nr.GET(\\\"/\\\", handler)                       // ← Handler creates child spans\\n\\nCommon use cases that need the parent span:\\n\\n- Database transactions with tracing\\n\\n- Inter-service HTTP calls with trace propagation\\n\\n- Structured logging with trace IDs\\n\\n- Background jobs that need trace context\\n\\nYour example breaks all of these - they'd have no parent span.\\n\\n3. Users can control span isolation themselves \\n\\nIf a user doesn't want their spans to be children of otelgin's span, they can do exactly what the defer does - but explicitly:\\n\\n```go\\n\\nvar tracer = otel.Tracer(instrumentationName)\\n\\nfunc myCustomMiddleware(c *gin.Context) {\\n\\n    ctx, span := tracer.Start(c.Request.Context(), \\\"myCustomMiddleware\\\")\\n\\n    defer span.End()\\n\\n    c.Next() // runs otelgin and other middleware\\n\\n    // Explicitly restore context if the user doesn't want child spans and since the user is in control of goroutines the onus is on them to do so safely (as it should be)  \\n\\n    c.Request = c.Request.WithContext(ctx)\\n\\n}\\n\\n```\\n\\nThis gives users control without the library making opinionated (and race-prone) decisions.\\n\\nEven if we agreed on the semantics, I'm not sure of a safe way of doing it from a library implementation.\\n\\nBottom line: The defer enforces an anti-pattern, breaks the common use case (otelgin as root span), prevents valid patterns (goroutines with trace context), and causes data races.\\n\\nUsers who need span isolation can manage it themselves without the library making unsafe assumptions.\\n\\nWhat do you think? I'm happy to add documentation showing how users can achieve span isolation if they need it. \\n\\n---\\n\\n**dmathieu** — 2025-10-14T08:42:01Z\\n\\nI disagree with this being a violation of Go's conventions (in the context of the middleware pattern, we don't flow forward. At the end of a middleware, we go back to its parent).\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"context form a tree success call to withvalu withcancel withdeadlin or withtimeout deriv new context context are meant to flow forward not be restor backward the librari shouldn t enforc this opinion 2 most user want otelgin earli in the chain i and i assum most user place otelgin a one of the first middlewar specif so child span can be creat from it r use otelgin middlewar my servic first creat root span r use loggingmiddlewar creat child span r use authmiddlewar creat child span r get handler handler creat child span common use case that need the parent span databas transact with trace inter servic http call with trace propag structur log with trace id background job that need trace context your exampl break all of these they d have no parent span 3 user can control span isol themselv if a user doesn t want their span to be child of otelgin s span they can do exact what the defer doe but explicit go var tracer otel tracer instrumentationnam func mycustommiddlewar c gin context ctx span tracer start c request context mycustommiddlewar defer span end c next run otelgin and other middlewar explicit restor context if the user doesn t want child span and sinc the user is in control of goroutin the onus is on them to do so safe a it should be c request c request withcontext ctx this give user control without the librari make opinion and race prone decis even if we agre on the semant i m not sure of a safe way of do it from a librari implement bottom line the defer enforc an anti pattern break the common use case otelgin a root span prevent valid pattern goroutin with trace context and caus data race user who need span isol can manag it themselv without the librari make unsaf assumpt what do you think i m happi to add document show how user can achiev span isol if they need it dmathieu 2025 10 14t08 42 01z i disagre with this be a violat of go s convent in the context of the middlewar pattern we don t flow forward at the end of a middlewar we go back to it parent\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8753acb88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"id\": \"9ae5e4f55cbf7762\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.4072455769219989, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.31008949560285565, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6339431, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8753acb88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 33019, \"chunk_count\": 21, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:16\", \"token_count\": 10517, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-07]\\n\\n# Pull Request: otelgin: remove unneeded context save/restore to avoid data race (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#8014)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/8014  \\n\\n**Author**: nicksherron  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-10-14T04:01:24Z · **Updated**: 2025-10-17T10:42:07Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: closed  \\n\\n**Branch**: `fix/otelgin-data-race` → `main`  \\n\\n**Changes**: +83 / -10 across 2 files  \\n\\n**Labels**: —  \\n\\n**Milestone**: —\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThere seems to be absolutely no reason to save and restore the request context in a deferred function. The way it was done before could (and did) lead to a race condition because when c.Next() is called, the request context could be changed by another goroutine, and then the deferred function would modify the request while another goroutine is using it. \\n\\nI can't for the life of me figure out what benefit the previous code was trying to achieve, other than maybe trying to minimize the context size in memory, but that seems unnecessary and not worth the risk of a data race. Furthermore, I'm not even sure that said memory savings would pay off because when running `go build -gcflags=\\\"-m\\\"` against the current implementation you can see that context and request escapes to heap:\\n\\n```\\n\\n./gin.go:84:37: \\\"nil context\\\" escapes to heap\\n\\n./gin.go:84:37: new(http.Request) escapes to heap\\n\\n```\\n\\nThis is likely negligible but I figured I'd add it for more context, no pun intended 😉\\n\\nPerhaps the goal was not that of performance/memory savings but instead to \\\"restore\\\" the context. If so, this is also incorrect because in Gin, there's no need to restore the context - each request gets its own *gin.Context .\\n\\nFinally, this change actually more closely matches the [code cited](https://github.com/DataDog/dd-trace-go/blob/8fb554ff7cf694267f9077ae35e27ce4689ed8b6/contrib/gin-gonic/gin/gintrace.go) as the \\\"inspiration\\\" for the otelgin package. \\n\\nWithout this change, we unfortunately cannot run our tests with the race detector enabled and is not production ready due to not being goroutine safe.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src pr 07 pull request otelgin remov unneed context save restor to avoid data race open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 8014 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 8014 author nicksherron creat 2025 10 14t04 01 24z updat 2025 10 17t10 42 07z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state close branch fix otelgin data race main chang 83 10 across 2 file label mileston descript there seem to be absolut no reason to save and restor the request context in a defer function the way it wa done befor could and did lead to a race condit becaus when c next is call the request context could be chang by anoth goroutin and then the defer function would modifi the request while anoth goroutin is use it i can t for the life of me figur out what benefit the previous code wa tri to achiev other than mayb tri to minim the context size in memori but that seem unnecessari and not worth the risk of a data race furthermor i m not even sure that said memori save would pay off becaus when run go build gcflag m against the current implement you can see that context and request escap to heap gin go 84 37 nil context escap to heap gin go 84 37 new http request escap to heap this is like neglig but i figur i d add it for more context no pun intend perhap the goal wa not that of perform memori save but instead to restor the context if so this is also incorrect becaus in gin there s no need to restor the context each request get it own gin context final this chang actual more close match the code cite http github com datadog dd trace go blob 8fb554ff7cf694267f9077ae35e27ce4689ed8b6 contrib gin gonic gin gintrac go a the inspir for the otelgin packag without this chang we unfortun can not run our test with the race detector enabl and is not product readi due to not be goroutin safe\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8753acb88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"id\": \"a69b1eaa6d5ba704\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3779927581414831, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.2589354687735473, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6557931, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8753acb88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 33019, \"chunk_count\": 21, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:16\", \"token_count\": 10517, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"---\\n\\n**nicksherron** — 2025-10-14T04:43:31Z\\n\\nJust found an open 2 year old issue this would fix #4588 \\n\\n---\\n\\n**nicksherron** — 2025-10-14T04:56:41Z\\n\\nThanks for the quick response @flc1125 , but I would like to offer a rebuttal. \\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-07]\\n\\n# Pull Request: otelgin: remove unneeded context save/restore to avoid data race (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#8014)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/8014  \\n\\n**Author**: nicksherron  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-10-14T04:01:24Z · **Updated**: 2025-10-17T10:42:07Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: closed  \\n\\n**Branch**: `fix/otelgin-data-race` → `main`  \\n\\n**Changes**: +83 / -10 across 2 files  \\n\\n**Labels**: —  \\n\\n**Milestone**: —\\n\\n---\\n\\n## This PR Fixes an Existing Bug, Not Introducing New Safety Mechanisms\\n\\nI respectfully disagree with the characterization that this PR \\\"introduces mechanisms for concurrency safety.\\\" The opposite is true: this PR removes problematic code that causes a data race.\\n\\nThe current code has a real, reproducible race condition reported in issue #4588 (open for 2 years). The race detector fails consistently. This is not theoretical—it violates Go's memory model.\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-07]\\n\\n# Pull Request: otelgin: remove unneeded context save/restore to avoid data race (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#8014)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-con