rtant_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.37503744961801844, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.24135657088288345, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6869595, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8753acb88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 33019, \"chunk_count\": 21, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:16\", \"token_count\": 10517, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-07]\\n\\n# Pull Request: otelgin: remove unneeded context save/restore to avoid data race (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#8014)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/8014  \\n\\n**Author**: nicksherron  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-10-14T04:01:24Z · **Updated**: 2025-10-17T10:42:07Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: closed  \\n\\n**Branch**: `fix/otelgin-data-race` → `main`  \\n\\n**Changes**: +83 / -10 across 2 files  \\n\\n**Labels**: —  \\n\\n**Milestone**: —\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Users Cannot Fix This Themselves\\n\\n This is middleware code that users cannot work around without forking the library. The race happens inside otelgin.Middleware(). A user who wants to use otelgin AND pass race detection has no choice but to:\\n\\n  1. Fork this library\\n\\n  2. Apply this exact fix\\n\\n  3. Maintain their fork indefinitely\\n\\n  This is not \\\"leaving the decision to users\\\"—it's forcing users to fork or live with failing race detection.\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-07]\\n\\n# Pull Request: otelgin: remove unneeded context save/restore to avoid data race (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#8014)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/8014  \\n\\n**Author**: nicksherron  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-10-14T04:01:24Z · **Updated**: 2025-10-17T10:42:07Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: closed  \\n\\n**Branch**: `fix/otelgin-data-race` → `main`  \\n\\n**Changes**: +83 / -10 across 2 files  \\n\\n**Labels**: —  \\n\\n**Milestone**: —\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Precedent: This Project Has Fixed Similar Races Before\\n\\n  From the git history:\\n\\n  - #4577: \\\"otelgrpc: Fix data race in stats handlers\\\" (merged)\\n\\n  - #881: \\\"otelsarama: Fix WrapAsyncProducer race condition\\\" (merged)\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src pr 07 pull request otelgin remov unneed context save restor to avoid data race open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 8014 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 8014 author nicksherron creat 2025 10 14t04 01 24z updat 2025 10 17t10 42 07z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state close branch fix otelgin data race main chang 83 10 across 2 file label mileston user can not fix this themselv this is middlewar code that user can not work around without fork the librari the race happen insid otelgin middlewar a user who want to use otelgin and pas race detect ha no choic but to 1 fork this librari 2 appli this exact fix 3 maintain their fork indefinit this is not leav the decis to user it s forc user to fork or live with fail race detect sourc id src pr 07 pull request otelgin remov unneed context save restor to avoid data race open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 8014 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 8014 author nicksherron creat 2025 10 14t04 01 24z updat 2025 10 17t10 42 07z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state close branch fix otelgin data race main chang 83 10 across 2 file label mileston preced this project ha fix similar race befor from the git histori 4577 otelgrpc fix data race in stat handler merg 881 otelsarama fix wrapasyncproduc race condit merg\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8753acb88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"id\": \"c020b4557f49eb79\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3721491696180184, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.24135657088288345, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6773319, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8753acb88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 33019, \"chunk_count\": 21, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:16\", \"token_count\": 10517, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"> Could you turn your gist into a test that can run on CI, and add it to this PR?\\n\\nSure, I'd be happy to.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**flc1125** — 2025-10-14T07:42:26Z\\n\\n> ```go\\n\\n> }(c.Request.Context(), c.Writer.Status(), time.Since(start))\\n\\n>           //  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\\n\\n>           //  THIS RACES WITH otelgin's defer!\\n\\n> ```\\n\\nI believe my understanding aligns with yours. I approve this PR and agree with the changes.\\n\\nI'd like to clarify that the primary value isn't about \\\"fixing data race\\\". Rather, it removes unnecessary code that has unintended side effects.\\n\\ne.g., The defer restoration discards any context modifications made within the `otelgin` middleware chain (including downstream handlers).\\n\\n---\\n\\n**nicksherron** — 2025-10-14T07:47:23Z\\n\\n> > ```go\\n\\n> > }(c.Request.Context(), c.Writer.Status(), time.Since(start))\\n\\n> >           //  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\\n\\n> >           //  THIS RACES WITH otelgin's defer!\\n\\n> > ```\\n\\n> \\n\\n> I believe my understanding aligns with yours. I approve this PR and agree with the changes.\\n\\n> \\n\\n> I'd like to clarify that the primary value isn't about \\\"fixing data race\\\". Rather, it removes unnecessary code that has unintended side effects.\\n\\n> \\n\\n> e.g., The defer restoration discards any context modifications made within the `otelgin` middleware chain (including downstream handlers).\\n\\nSounds good, thank you for your time on this. I also added the test @dmathieu requested. If you want me to make any changes to it just let me know.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**codecov[bot]** — 2025-10-14T07:50:11Z\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-07]\\n\\n# Pull Request: otelgin: remove unneeded context save/restore to avoid data race (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#8014)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/8014  \\n\\n**Author**: nicksherron  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-10-14T04:01:24Z · **Updated**: 2025-10-17T10:42:07Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"could you turn your gist into a test that can run on ci and add it to this pr sure i d be happi to flc1125 2025 10 14t07 42 26z go c request context c writer status time sinc start this race with otelgin s defer i believ my understand align with your i approv this pr and agre with the chang i d like to clarifi that the primari valu isn t about fix data race rather it remov unnecessari code that ha unintend side effect e g the defer restor discard ani context modif made within the otelgin middlewar chain includ downstream handler nicksherron 2025 10 14t07 47 23z go c request context c writer status time sinc start this race with otelgin s defer i believ my understand align with your i approv this pr and agre with the chang i d like to clarifi that the primari valu isn t about fix data race rather it remov unnecessari code that ha unintend side effect e g the defer restor discard ani context modif made within the otelgin middlewar chain includ downstream handler sound good thank you for your time on this i also ad the test dmathieu request if you want me to make ani chang to it just let me know codecov bot 2025 10 14t07 50 11z sourc id src pr 07 pull request otelgin remov unneed context save restor to avoid data race open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 8014 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 8014 author nicksherron creat 2025 10 14t04 01 24z updat 2025 10 17t10 42 07z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8753acb88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"id\": \"998f12a39803f3d9\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3717065196180184, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.24135657088288345, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6758564, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8753acb88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 33019, \"chunk_count\": 21, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:16\", \"token_count\": 10517, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"  These fixes were accepted because data races are bugs, not \\\"concurrency mechanisms left to users.\\\"\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-07]\\n\\n# Pull Request: otelgin: remove unneeded context save/restore to avoid data race (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#8014)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/8014  \\n\\n**Author**: nicksherron  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-10-14T04:01:24Z · **Updated**: 2025-10-17T10:42:07Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: closed  \\n\\n**Branch**: `fix/otelgin-data-race` → `main`  \\n\\n**Changes**: +83 / -10 across 2 files  \\n\\n**Labels**: —  \\n\\n**Milestone**: —\\n\\n---\\n\\n## The Race Is Real and Reproducible\\n\\n  From issue #4588:\\n\\n  WARNING: DATA RACE\\n\\n  Write at 0x... by goroutine X:\\n\\n    [defer in Middleware]\\n\\n  Read at 0x... by goroutine Y:\\n\\n    [user handler accessing context]\\n\\n  This is undefined behavior. The Go memory model states: \\\"Programs that modify data being simultaneously accessed by multiple goroutines must serialize such access.\\\"\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-07]\\n\\n# Pull Request: otelgin: remove unneeded context save/restore to avoid data race (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#8014)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/8014  \\n\\n**Author**: nicksherron  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-10-14T04:01:24Z · **Updated**: 2025-10-17T10:42:07Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: closed  \\n\\n**Branch**: `fix/otelgin-data-race` → `main`  \\n\\n**Changes**: +83 / -10 across 2 files  \\n\\n**Labels**: —  \\n\\n**Milestone**: —\\n\\n---\\n\\n## The Fix is Correct\\n\\n  The fix simply removes dead code:\\n\\n```go\\n\\n  // Before: Save and restore (unnecessary)\\n\\n  savedCtx := c.Request.Context()\\n\\n  defer func() { c.Request = c.Request.WithContext(savedCtx) }()\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"these fix were accept becaus data race are bug not concurr mechan left to user sourc id src pr 07 pull request otelgin remov unneed context save restor to avoid data race open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 8014 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 8014 author nicksherron creat 2025 10 14t04 01 24z updat 2025 10 17t10 42 07z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state close branch fix otelgin data race main chang 83 10 across 2 file label mileston the race is real and reproduc from issu 4588 warn data race write at 0x by goroutin x defer in middlewar read at 0x by goroutin y user handler access context this is undefin behavior the go memori model state program that modifi data be simultan access by multipl goroutin must serial such access sourc id src pr 07 pull request otelgin remov unneed context save restor to avoid data race open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 8014 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 8014 author nicksherron creat 2025 10 14t04 01 24z updat 2025 10 17t10 42 07z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state close branch fix otelgin data race main chang 83 10 across 2 file label mileston the fix is correct the fix simpli remov dead code go befor save and restor unnecessari savedctx c request context defer func c request c request withcontext savedctx\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8753acb88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"id\": \"b40b58fd0d2fea42\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3651914496180184, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.24135657088288345, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6541395, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8753acb88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 33019, \"chunk_count\": 21, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:16\", \"token_count\": 10517, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-07]\\n\\n# Pull Request: otelgin: remove unneeded context save/restore to avoid data race (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#8014)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/8014  \\n\\n**Author**: nicksherron  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-10-14T04:01:24Z · **Updated**: 2025-10-17T10:42:07Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: closed  \\n\\n**Branch**: `fix/otelgin-data-race` → `main`  \\n\\n**Changes**: +83 / -10 across 2 files  \\n\\n**Labels**: —  \\n\\n**Milestone**: —\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Discussion (27)\\n\\n**linux-foundation-easycla[bot]** — 2025-10-14T04:01:31Z\\n\\n<a href=\\\"https://easycla.lfx.linuxfoundation.org/#/?version=2\\\"><img src=\\\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/cla-project-logo-prod/cla-signed.svg?v=2\\\" alt=\\\"CLA Signed\\\" align=\\\"left\\\" height=\\\"28\\\" width=\\\"328\\\" ></a><br/><br />The committers listed above are authorized under a signed CLA.<ul><li>:white_check_mark: login: nicksherron / name: Nick Sherron  (43d6c1b5f0c27c73a83543d0f681e2dc766d86dc, 6c560fe0a618c400f5961126b3daf71074a98113, ebe29b975966edee33e7c0e2fdcca7c89710fd63)</li></ul>\\n\\n---\\n\\n**flc1125** — 2025-10-14T04:35:20Z\\n\\nThe current changes do not guarantee thread safety.\\n\\nAdditionally, I lean towards the view that for infrastructure-level components or frameworks, there is no need to consider the concurrency safety of `req.WithContext` and `req.Context()`.\\n\\nOnce these components introduce certain mechanisms for concurrency safety, it may lead to performance degradation.\\n\\nFor users pursuing high performance, such performance degradation is unacceptable. Moreover, once implemented, users have no choice but to use these mechanisms.\\n\\nTherefore, I prefer to leave the decision of whether to ensure concurrency safety to the users themselves, and let them implement these mechanisms on their own.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src pr 07 pull request otelgin remov unneed context save restor to avoid data race open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 8014 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 8014 author nicksherron creat 2025 10 14t04 01 24z updat 2025 10 17t10 42 07z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state close branch fix otelgin data race main chang 83 10 across 2 file label mileston discuss 27 linux foundat easycla bot 2025 10 14t04 01 31z a href http easycla lfx linuxfound org version 2 img src http s3 amazonaw com cla project logo prod cla sign svg v2 alt cla sign align left height 28 width 328 a br br the committ list abov are author under a sign cla ul li white _ check _ mark login nicksherron name nick sherron 43d6c1b5f0c27c73a83543d0f681e2dc766d86dc 6c560fe0a618c400f5961126b3daf71074a98113 ebe29b975966edee33e7c0e2fdcca7c89710fd63 li ul flc1125 2025 10 14t04 35 20z the current chang do not guarante thread safeti addit i lean toward the view that for infrastructur level compon or framework there is no need to consid the concurr safeti of req withcontext and req context onc these compon introduc certain mechan for concurr safeti it may lead to perform degrad for user pursu high perform such perform degrad is unaccept moreov onc implement user have no choic but to use these mechan therefor i prefer to leav the decis of whether to ensur concurr safeti to the user themselv and let them implement these mechan on their own\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8753acb88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"id\": \"9d57dc1fb2041765\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3633006396180184, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.24135657088288345, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6478368, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8753acb88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 33019, \"chunk_count\": 21, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:16\", \"token_count\": 10517, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"      router.Use(asyncLoggingMiddleware())\\n\\n      router.POST(\\\"/api/orders\\\", createOrder)\\n\\n      router.Run(\\\":8080\\\")\\n\\n  }\\n\\n  // Async logging middleware - BREAKS with otelgin's defer pattern\\n\\n  func asyncLoggingMiddleware() gin.HandlerFunc {\\n\\n      logger := zap.NewProduction()\\n\\n      return func(c *gin.Context) {\\n\\n          start := time.Now()\\n\\n          path := c.Request.URL.Path\\n\\n          method := c.Request.Method\\n\\n          // Process request\\n\\n          c.Next()\\n\\n          // Log asynchronously to avoid blocking response\\n\\n          // This is THE standard pattern for production logging\\n\\n          go func(ctx context.Context, statusCode int, duration time.Duration) {\\n\\n              // Extract trace context for correlation\\n\\n              span := trace.SpanFromContext(ctx)\\n\\n              traceID := span.SpanContext().TraceID().String()\\n\\n              spanID := span.SpanContext().SpanID().String()\\n\\n              // Write structured log with trace correlation\\n\\n              logger.Info(\\\"http_request\\\",\\n\\n                  zap.String(\\\"method\\\", method),\\n\\n                  zap.String(\\\"path\\\", path),\\n\\n                  zap.Int(\\\"status\\\", statusCode),\\n\\n                  zap.Duration(\\\"duration\\\", duration),\\n\\n                  zap.String(\\\"trace_id\\\", traceID),    // ← Links logs to traces\\n\\n                  zap.String(\\\"span_id\\\", spanID),\\n\\n              )\\n\\n              // Could also send to external logging service here\\n\\n              // sendToDatadog(ctx, logEntry)\\n\\n              // sendToCloudWatch(ctx, logEntry)\\n\\n          }(c.Request.Context(), c.Writer.Status(), time.Since(start))\\n\\n          //  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\\n\\n          //  THIS RACES WITH otelgin's defer!\\n\\n      }\\n\\n  }\\n\\n  func createOrder(c *gin.Context) {\\n\\n      var order Order\\n\\n      if err := c.BindJSON(&order); err != nil {\\n\\n          c.JSON(400, gin.H{\\\"error\\\": err.Error()})\\n\\n          return\\n\\n      }\\n\\n      // Process order...\\n\\n      c.JSON(201, order)\\n\\n  }\\n\\n  ```\\n\\n---\\n\\n**nicksherron** — 2025-10-14T06:58:23Z\\n\\nHopefully that provides enough evidence to support my claim which is that **the spurious defer code is prone to data races when used in a project with typical gin server patterns** and this PR fixes it.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**dmathieu** — 2025-10-14T07:26:23Z\\n\\nCould you turn your gist into a test that can run on CI, and add it to this PR?\\n\\n---\\n\\n**nicksherron** — 2025-10-14T07:27:58Z\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"router use asyncloggingmiddlewar router post api order createord router run 8080 async log middlewar break with otelgin s defer pattern func asyncloggingmiddlewar gin handlerfunc logger zap newproduct return func c gin context start time now path c request url path method c request method process request c next log asynchron to avoid block respons this is the standard pattern for product log go func ctx context context statuscod int durat time durat extract trace context for correl span trace spanfromcontext ctx traceid span spancontext traceid string spanid span spancontext spanid string write structur log with trace correl logger info http _ request zap string method method zap string path path zap int status statuscod zap durat durat durat zap string trace _ id traceid link log to trace zap string span _ id spanid could also send to extern log servic here sendtodatadog ctx logentri sendtocloudwatch ctx logentri c request context c writer status time sinc start this race with otelgin s defer func createord c gin context var order order if err c bindjson order err nil c json 400 gin h error err error return process order c json 201 order nicksherron 2025 10 14t06 58 23z hope that provid enough evid to support my claim which is that the spurious defer code is prone to data race when use in a project with typic gin server pattern and this pr fix it dmathieu 2025 10 14t07 26 23z could you turn your gist into a test that can run on ci and add it to this pr nicksherron 2025 10 14t07 27 58z\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8753acb88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"id\": \"2eb41ec8a7c42ad2\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3603833106180184, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.24135657088288345, \"vector_similarity\": 0.63811237, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8753acb88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 33019, \"chunk_count\": 21, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:16\", \"token_count\": 10517, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9