23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:16\", \"token_count\": 10517, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"  These fixes were accepted because data races are bugs, not \\\"concurrency mechanisms left to users.\\\"\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-07]\\n\\n# Pull Request: otelgin: remove unneeded context save/restore to avoid data race (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#8014)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/8014  \\n\\n**Author**: nicksherron  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-10-14T04:01:24Z · **Updated**: 2025-10-17T10:42:07Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: closed  \\n\\n**Branch**: `fix/otelgin-data-race` → `main`  \\n\\n**Changes**: +83 / -10 across 2 files  \\n\\n**Labels**: —  \\n\\n**Milestone**: —\\n\\n---\\n\\n## The Race Is Real and Reproducible\\n\\n  From issue #4588:\\n\\n  WARNING: DATA RACE\\n\\n  Write at 0x... by goroutine X:\\n\\n    [defer in Middleware]\\n\\n  Read at 0x... by goroutine Y:\\n\\n    [user handler accessing context]\\n\\n  This is undefined behavior. The Go memory model states: \\\"Programs that modify data being simultaneously accessed by multiple goroutines must serialize such access.\\\"\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-07]\\n\\n# Pull Request: otelgin: remove unneeded context save/restore to avoid data race (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#8014)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/8014  \\n\\n**Author**: nicksherron  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-10-14T04:01:24Z · **Updated**: 2025-10-17T10:42:07Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: closed  \\n\\n**Branch**: `fix/otelgin-data-race` → `main`  \\n\\n**Changes**: +83 / -10 across 2 files  \\n\\n**Labels**: —  \\n\\n**Milestone**: —\\n\\n---\\n\\n## The Fix is Correct\\n\\n  The fix simply removes dead code:\\n\\n```go\\n\\n  // Before: Save and restore (unnecessary)\\n\\n  savedCtx := c.Request.Context()\\n\\n  defer func() { c.Request = c.Request.WithContext(savedCtx) }()\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"these fix were accept becaus data race are bug not concurr mechan left to user sourc id src pr 07 pull request otelgin remov unneed context save restor to avoid data race open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 8014 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 8014 author nicksherron creat 2025 10 14t04 01 24z updat 2025 10 17t10 42 07z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state close branch fix otelgin data race main chang 83 10 across 2 file label mileston the race is real and reproduc from issu 4588 warn data race write at 0x by goroutin x defer in middlewar read at 0x by goroutin y user handler access context this is undefin behavior the go memori model state program that modifi data be simultan access by multipl goroutin must serial such access sourc id src pr 07 pull request otelgin remov unneed context save restor to avoid data race open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 8014 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 8014 author nicksherron creat 2025 10 14t04 01 24z updat 2025 10 17t10 42 07z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state close branch fix otelgin data race main chang 83 10 across 2 file label mileston the fix is correct the fix simpli remov dead code go befor save and restor unnecessari savedctx c request context defer func c request c request withcontext savedctx\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8753acb88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"id\": \"b40b58fd0d2fea42\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.34327812424045606, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.14705426320065157, \"vector_similarity\": 0.8011338, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8753acb88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 33019, \"chunk_count\": 21, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:16\", \"token_count\": 10517, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"---\\n\\n**nicksherron** — 2025-10-14T04:43:31Z\\n\\nJust found an open 2 year old issue this would fix #4588 \\n\\n---\\n\\n**nicksherron** — 2025-10-14T04:56:41Z\\n\\nThanks for the quick response @flc1125 , but I would like to offer a rebuttal. \\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-07]\\n\\n# Pull Request: otelgin: remove unneeded context save/restore to avoid data race (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#8014)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/8014  \\n\\n**Author**: nicksherron  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-10-14T04:01:24Z · **Updated**: 2025-10-17T10:42:07Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: closed  \\n\\n**Branch**: `fix/otelgin-data-race` → `main`  \\n\\n**Changes**: +83 / -10 across 2 files  \\n\\n**Labels**: —  \\n\\n**Milestone**: —\\n\\n---\\n\\n## This PR Fixes an Existing Bug, Not Introducing New Safety Mechanisms\\n\\nI respectfully disagree with the characterization that this PR \\\"introduces mechanisms for concurrency safety.\\\" The opposite is true: this PR removes problematic code that causes a data race.\\n\\nThe current code has a real, reproducible race condition reported in issue #4588 (open for 2 years). The race detector fails consistently. This is not theoretical—it violates Go's memory model.\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-07]\\n\\n# Pull Request: otelgin: remove unneeded context save/restore to avoid data race (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#8014)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/8014  \\n\\n**Author**: nicksherron  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-10-14T04:01:24Z · **Updated**: 2025-10-17T10:42:07Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: closed  \\n\\n**Branch**: `fix/otelgin-data-race` → `main`  \\n\\n**Changes**: +83 / -10 across 2 files  \\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"nicksherron 2025 10 14t04 43 31z just found an open 2 year old issu this would fix 4588 nicksherron 2025 10 14t04 56 41z thank for the quick respons flc1125 but i would like to offer a rebutt sourc id src pr 07 pull request otelgin remov unneed context save restor to avoid data race open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 8014 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 8014 author nicksherron creat 2025 10 14t04 01 24z updat 2025 10 17t10 42 07z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state close branch fix otelgin data race main chang 83 10 across 2 file label mileston this pr fix an exist bug not introduc new safeti mechan i respect disagre with the character that this pr introduc mechan for concurr safeti the opposit is true this pr remov problemat code that caus a data race the current code ha a real reproduc race condit report in issu 4588 open for 2 year the race detector fail consist this is not theoret it violat go s memori model sourc id src pr 07 pull request otelgin remov unneed context save restor to avoid data race open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 8014 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 8014 author nicksherron creat 2025 10 14t04 01 24z updat 2025 10 17t10 42 07z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state close branch fix otelgin data race main chang 83 10 across 2 file\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8753acb88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"id\": \"79dd2c776e5b2e7f\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3432152022404561, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.14705426320065157, \"vector_similarity\": 0.80092406, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8753acb88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 33019, \"chunk_count\": 21, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:16\", \"token_count\": 10517, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-07]\\n\\n# Pull Request: otelgin: remove unneeded context save/restore to avoid data race (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#8014)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/8014  \\n\\n**Author**: nicksherron  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-10-14T04:01:24Z · **Updated**: 2025-10-17T10:42:07Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: closed  \\n\\n**Branch**: `fix/otelgin-data-race` → `main`  \\n\\n**Changes**: +83 / -10 across 2 files  \\n\\n**Labels**: —  \\n\\n**Milestone**: —\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Discussion (27)\\n\\n**linux-foundation-easycla[bot]** — 2025-10-14T04:01:31Z\\n\\n<a href=\\\"https://easycla.lfx.linuxfoundation.org/#/?version=2\\\"><img src=\\\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/cla-project-logo-prod/cla-signed.svg?v=2\\\" alt=\\\"CLA Signed\\\" align=\\\"left\\\" height=\\\"28\\\" width=\\\"328\\\" ></a><br/><br />The committers listed above are authorized under a signed CLA.<ul><li>:white_check_mark: login: nicksherron / name: Nick Sherron  (43d6c1b5f0c27c73a83543d0f681e2dc766d86dc, 6c560fe0a618c400f5961126b3daf71074a98113, ebe29b975966edee33e7c0e2fdcca7c89710fd63)</li></ul>\\n\\n---\\n\\n**flc1125** — 2025-10-14T04:35:20Z\\n\\nThe current changes do not guarantee thread safety.\\n\\nAdditionally, I lean towards the view that for infrastructure-level components or frameworks, there is no need to consider the concurrency safety of `req.WithContext` and `req.Context()`.\\n\\nOnce these components introduce certain mechanisms for concurrency safety, it may lead to performance degradation.\\n\\nFor users pursuing high performance, such performance degradation is unacceptable. Moreover, once implemented, users have no choice but to use these mechanisms.\\n\\nTherefore, I prefer to leave the decision of whether to ensure concurrency safety to the users themselves, and let them implement these mechanisms on their own.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src pr 07 pull request otelgin remov unneed context save restor to avoid data race open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 8014 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 8014 author nicksherron creat 2025 10 14t04 01 24z updat 2025 10 17t10 42 07z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state close branch fix otelgin data race main chang 83 10 across 2 file label mileston discuss 27 linux foundat easycla bot 2025 10 14t04 01 31z a href http easycla lfx linuxfound org version 2 img src http s3 amazonaw com cla project logo prod cla sign svg v2 alt cla sign align left height 28 width 328 a br br the committ list abov are author under a sign cla ul li white _ check _ mark login nicksherron name nick sherron 43d6c1b5f0c27c73a83543d0f681e2dc766d86dc 6c560fe0a618c400f5961126b3daf71074a98113 ebe29b975966edee33e7c0e2fdcca7c89710fd63 li ul flc1125 2025 10 14t04 35 20z the current chang do not guarante thread safeti addit i lean toward the view that for infrastructur level compon or framework there is no need to consid the concurr safeti of req withcontext and req context onc these compon introduc certain mechan for concurr safeti it may lead to perform degrad for user pursu high perform such perform degrad is unaccept moreov onc implement user have no choic but to use these mechan therefor i prefer to leav the decis of whether to ensur concurr safeti to the user themselv and let them implement these mechan on their own\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8753acb88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"id\": \"9d57dc1fb2041765\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3409363242404561, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.14705426320065157, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7933278, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8753acb88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 33019, \"chunk_count\": 21, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:16\", \"token_count\": 10517, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Labels**: —  \\n\\n**Milestone**: —\\n\\n---\\n\\n## The Defer Provides No Benefit\\n\\nLet's analyze what the current code does:\\n\\n```go\\n\\n  savedCtx := c.Request.Context()\\n\\n  defer func() {\\n\\n      c.Request = c.Request.WithContext(savedCtx)  // ← Restores AFTER request completes\\n\\n  }()\\n\\n  ctx := cfg.Propagators.Extract(savedCtx, propagation.HeaderCarrier(c.Request.Header))\\n\\n  // ...\\n\\n  c.Request = c.Request.WithContext(ctx)  // ← Sets new context\\n\\n  c.Next()  // ← Processes request\\n\\n  // When we return, defer runs and \\\"restores\\\" the old context\\n\\n```\\n\\n  Question: Why restore the context after the request is complete?\\n\\n  - After c.Next() returns, the request has been fully processed\\n\\n  - Gin doesn't reuse *gin.Context instances across requests\\n\\n  - Downstream handlers may spawn goroutines that read c.Request.Context()\\n\\n  - The deferred write to c.Request races with those goroutine reads\\n\\n  - There is no code that benefits from this restoration\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-07]\\n\\n# Pull Request: otelgin: remove unneeded context save/restore to avoid data race (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#8014)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/8014  \\n\\n**Author**: nicksherron  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-10-14T04:01:24Z · **Updated**: 2025-10-17T10:42:07Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: closed  \\n\\n**Branch**: `fix/otelgin-data-race` → `main`  \\n\\n**Changes**: +83 / -10 across 2 files  \\n\\n**Labels**: —  \\n\\n**Milestone**: —\\n\\n---\\n\\n## The Performance Argument is Backwards\\n\\nThe current code with the defer is slower than the fix:\\n\\n  Current code overhead:\\n\\n  - Allocates closure for defer\\n\\n  - Saves context reference\\n\\n  - Executes deferred function on return\\n\\n  - Calls WithContext() twice (once to set, once to \\\"restore\\\")\\n\\n  Fixed code:\\n\\n  - No defer\\n\\n  - No closure allocation\\n\\n  - One fewer WithContext() call\\n\\n  - No unnecessary context copy\\n\\n Benchmark comparison (removing defer should show improvement):\\n\\n  -  Current: ~3 allocations per request\\n\\n  -  Fixed:   ~2 allocations per request\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"label mileston the defer provid no benefit let s analyz what the current code doe go savedctx c request context defer func c request c request withcontext savedctx restor after request complet ctx cfg propag extract savedctx propag headercarri c request header c request c request withcontext ctx set new context c next process request when we return defer run and restor the old context question whi restor the context after the request is complet after c next return the request ha been fulli process gin doesn t reus gin context instanc across request downstream handler may spawn goroutin that read c request context the defer write to c request race with those goroutin read there is no code that benefit from this restor sourc id src pr 07 pull request otelgin remov unneed context save restor to avoid data race open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 8014 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 8014 author nicksherron creat 2025 10 14t04 01 24z updat 2025 10 17t10 42 07z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state close branch fix otelgin data race main chang 83 10 across 2 file label mileston the perform argument is backward the current code with the defer is slower than the fix current code overhead alloc closur for defer save context refer execut defer function on return call withcontext twice onc to set onc to restor fix code no defer no closur alloc one fewer withcontext call no unnecessari context copi benchmark comparison remov defer should show improv current 3 alloc per request fix 2 alloc per request\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8753acb88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"id\": \"0e4329537c0aa36a\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3355804842404561, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.14705426320065157, \"vector_similarity\": 0.775475, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8753acb88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 33019, \"chunk_count\": 21, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:16\", \"token_count\": 10517, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"  ctx := cfg.Propagators.Extract(savedCtx, ...)\\n\\n  // After: Use context directly (correct)\\n\\n  reqCtx := c.Request.Context()\\n\\n  ctx := cfg.Propagators.Extract(reqCtx, ...)\\n\\n```\\n\\n  The behavior is identical except:\\n\\n  -  No race condition\\n\\n  -  Better performance\\n\\n  -  Simpler code\\n\\n  -  Tests pass with -race\\n\\n  Conclusion\\n\\n  This is a straightforward bug fix that:\\n\\n  1. Removes unnecessary code that causes a race\\n\\n  2. Improves performance (fewer allocations, no defer overhead)\\n\\n  3. Fixes a 2-year-old issue (#4588)\\n\\n  4. Follows precedent from previous race fixes in this project\\n\\n  5. Enables CI to enforce race-free code\\n\\n  There is no downside to this change, and significant benefits. I respectfully request approval to merge.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**akats7** — 2025-10-14T04:58:07Z\\n\\nHi @nicksherron, \\n\\nIt's a fair question, I also don't really see the benefit of it, I'm going to assume it was added for hygiene to avoid leaking the modifications out of the intended request's middleware chain.\\n\\n@flc1125 what are your thoughts, even if it doesn't provide thread safety it does seem valid\\n\\n---\\n\\n**flc1125** — 2025-10-14T05:01:16Z\\n\\n> I'm going to assume it was added for hygiene to avoid leaking the modifications out of the intended request's middleware chain.\\n\\nI agree with this situation.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**nicksherron** — 2025-10-14T05:06:09Z\\n\\nI'm confused about this \\\"doesn't provide thread safety\\\" claim. I'm starring at a test failure due to data race when running `go test -race`  in one of my projects that clearly points the finger to the code I removed as being the culprit. When I do a `go mod -replace` using my change in this PR the race goes away. \\n\\n---\\n\\n**flc1125** — 2025-10-14T05:09:52Z\\n\\n> I'm confused about this \\\"doesn't provide thread safety\\\" claim. I'm starring at a test failure due to data race when running `go test -race` in one of my projects that clearly points the finger to the code I removed as being the culprit. When I do a `go mod -replace` using my change in this PR the race goes away.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"ctx cfg propag extract savedctx after use context direct correct reqctx c request context ctx cfg propag extract reqctx the behavior is ident except no race condit better perform simpler code test pas with race conclus this is a straightforward bug fix that 1 remov unnecessari code that caus a race 2 improv perform fewer alloc no defer overhead 3 fix a2 year old issu 4588 4 follow preced from previous race fix in this project 5 enabl ci to enforc race free code there is no downsid to this chang and signific benefit i respect request approv to merg akats7 2025 10 14t04 58 07z hi nicksherron it s a fair question i also don t realli see the benefit of it i m go to assum it wa ad for hygien to avoid leak the modif out of the intend request s middlewar chain flc1125 what are your thought even if it doesn t provid thread safeti it doe seem valid flc1125 2025 10 14t05 01 16z i m go to assum it wa ad for hygien to avoid leak the modif out of the intend request s middlewar chain i agre with this situat nicksherron 2025 10 14t05 06 09z i m confus about this doesn t provid thread safeti claim i m star at a test failur due to data race when run go test race in one of my project that clear point the finger to the code i remov a be the culprit when i do a go mod replac use my chang in this pr the race go away flc1125 2025 10 14t05 09 52z i m confus about this doesn t provid thread safeti claim i m star at a test failur due to data race when run go test race in one of my project that clear point the finger to the code i remov a be the culprit when i do a go mod replac use my chang in this pr the race go away\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8753acb88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"id\": \"cad80d2ecd6e532f\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3292703622404561, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.14705426320065157, \"vector_similarity\": 0.75444126, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8753acb88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 33019, \"chunk_count\": 21, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:16\", \"token_count\": 10517, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"> Could you turn your gist into a test that can run on CI, and add it to this PR?\\n\\nSure, I'd be happy to.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**flc1125** — 2025-10-14T07:42:26Z\\n\\n> ```go\\n\\n> }(c.Request.Context(), c.Writer.Status(), time.Since(start))\\n\\n>           //  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\\n\\n>           //  THIS RACES WITH otelgin's defer!\\n\\n> ```\\n\\nI believe my understanding aligns with yours. I approve this PR and agree with the changes.\\n\\nI'd like to clarify that the primary value isn't about \\\"fixing data race\\\". Rather, it removes unnecessary code that has unintended side effects.\\n\\ne.g., The defer restoration discards any context modifications made within the `otelgin` middleware chain (including downstream handlers).\\n\\n---\\n\\n**nicksherron** — 2025-10-14T07:47:23Z\\n\\n> > ```go\\n\\n> > }(c.Request.Context(), c.Writer.Status(), time.Since(start))\\n\\n> >           //  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\\n\\n> >           //  THIS RACES WITH otelgin's defer!\\n\\n> > ```\\n\\n> \\n\\n> I believe my understanding aligns with yours. I approve this PR and agree with the changes.\\n\\n> \\n\\n> I'd like to clarify that the primary value isn't about \\\"fixing data race\\\". Rather, it removes unnecessary code that has unintended side effects.\\n\\n> \\n\\n> e.g., The defer restoration discards any context modifications made within the `otelgin` middleware chain (including downstream handlers).\\n\\nSounds good, thank you for your time on this. I also added the test @dmathieu requested. If you want me to make any changes to it just let me know.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**codecov[bot]** — 2025-10-14T07:50:11Z\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-07]\\n\\n# Pull Request: otelgin: remove unneeded context save/restore to avoid data race (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#8014)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/8014  \\n\\n**Author**: nicksherron  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-10-14T04:01:24Z · **Updated**: 2025-10-17T10:42:07Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"could you turn your gist into a test that can run on ci and add it to this pr sure i d be happi to flc1125 2025 10 14t07 42 26z go c request context c writer status time sinc start this race with otelgin s defer i believ my understand align with your i approv this pr and agre with the chang i d like to clarifi that the primari valu isn t about fix data race rather it remov unnecessari code that ha unintend side effect e g the defer restor discard ani context modif made within the otelgin middlewar chain includ downstream handler nicksherron 2025 10 14t07 47 23z go c request context c writer status time sinc start this race with otelgin s defer i believ my understand align with your i approv this pr and agre with the chang i d like to clarifi that the primari valu isn t about fix data race rather it remov unnecessari code that ha unintend side effect e g the defer restor discard ani context modif made within the otelgin middlewar chain includ downstream handler sound good thank you for your time on this i also ad the test dmathieu request if you want me to make ani chang to it just let me know codecov bot 2025 10 14t07 50 11z sourc id src pr 07 pull request otelgin remov unneed context save restor to avoid data race open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 8014 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 8014 author nicksherron creat 2025 10 14t04 01 24z updat 2025 10 17t10 42 07z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8753acb88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"id\": \"998f12a39803f3d9\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3219411977487998, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.1247957253554283, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7819473, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8753acb88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 33019, \"chunk_count\": 21, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:16\", \"token_count\": 10517, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"> \\\"Contexts form a tree... Successive calls to WithValue, WithCancel, WithDeadline, or WithTimeout derive new contexts.\\\"\\n\\nContexts are meant to flow forward, not be \\\"restored\\\" backward. The library shouldn't enforce this opinion.\\n\\n2. Most users want otelgin early in the chain\\n\\nI (and I assume most users) place otelgin as one of the first middleware specifically so child spans can be created from it:\\n\\nr.Use(otelgin.Middleware(\\\"my-service\\\"))  // ← First - creates root span\\n\\nr.Use(loggingMiddleware)                  // ← Creates child spans\\n\\nr.Use(authMiddleware)                     // ← Creates child spans\\n\\nr.GET(\\\"/\\\", handler)                       // ← Handler creates child spans\\n\\nCommon use cases that need the parent span:\\n\\n- Database transactions with tracing\\n\\n- Inter-service HTTP calls with trace propagation\\n\\n- Structured logging with trace IDs\\n\\n- Background jobs that need trace context\\n\\nYour example breaks all of these - they'd have no parent span.\\n\\n3. Users can control span isolation themselves \\n\\nIf a user doesn't want their spans to be children of otelgin's span, they can do exactly what the defer does - but explicitly:\\n\\n```go\\n\\nvar tracer = otel.Tracer(instrumentationName)\\n\\nfunc myCustomMiddleware(c *gin.Context) {\\n\\n    ctx, span := tracer.Start(c.Request.Context(), \\\"myCustomMiddleware\\\")\\n\\n    defer span.End()\\n\\n    c.Next() // runs otelgin and other middleware\\n\\n    // Explicitly restore context if the user doesn't want child spans and since the user is in control of goroutines the onus is on them to do so safely (as it should be)  \\n\\n    c.Request = c.Request.WithContext(ctx)\\n\\n}\\n\\n```\\n\\nThis gives users control without the library making opinionated (and race-prone) decisions.\\n\\nEven if we agreed on the semantics, I'm not sure of a safe way of doing it from a library implementation.\\n\\nBottom line: The defer enforces an anti-pattern, breaks the common use case (otelgin as root span), prevents valid patterns (goroutines with trace context), and causes data races.\\n\\nUsers who need span isolation can manage it themselves without the library making unsafe assumptions.\\n\\nWhat do you think? I'm happy to add documentation showing how users can achieve span isolation if they need it. \\n\\n---\\n\\n**dmathieu** — 2025-10-14T08:42:01Z\\n\\nI disagree with this being a violation of Go's conventions (in the context of the middleware pattern, we don't flow forward. At the end of a middleware, we go back to its parent).\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"context form a tree success call to withvalu withcancel withdeadlin or withtimeout deriv new context context are meant to flow forward not be restor backward the librari shouldn t enforc this opinion 2 most user want otelgin earli in the chain i and i assum most user place otelgin a one of the first middlewar specif so child span can be creat from it r use otelgin middlewar my servic first creat root span r use loggingmiddlewar creat child span r use authmiddlewar creat child span r get handler handler creat child span common use case that need the parent span databas transact with trace inter servic http call with trace propag structur log with trace id background job that need trace context your exampl break all of these they d have no parent span 3 user can control span isol themselv if a user doesn t want their span to be child of otelgin s span they can do exact what the defer doe but explicit go var tracer otel tracer instrumentationnam func mycustommiddlewar c gin context ctx span tracer start c request context mycustommiddlewar defer span end c next run otelgin and other middlewar explicit restor context if the user doesn t want child span and sinc the user is in control of goroutin the onus is on them to do so safe a it should be c request c request withcontext ctx this give user control without the librari make opinion and race prone decis even if we agre on the semant i m not sure of a safe way of do it from a librari implement bottom line the defer enforc an anti pattern break the common use case otelgin a root span prevent valid pattern goroutin with trace context and caus data race user who need span isol can manag it themselv without the librari make unsaf assumpt what do you think i m happi to add document show how user can achiev span isol if they need it dmathieu 2025 10 14t08 42 01z i disagre with this be a violat of go s convent in the context of the middlewar pattern we don t flow forward at the end of a middlewar we go back to it parent\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8753acb88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"id\": \"9ae5e4f55cbf7762\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3196262957487998, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.1247957253554283, \"vector_similarity\": 0.77423096, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8753acb88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 33019, \"chunk_count\": 21, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:16\", \"token_count\": 10517, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}], \"pagination\": {\"page\": 1, \"page_size\": 10, \"total_chunks\": 70, \"total_pages\": 7}, \"query_info\": {\"question\": \"opentelemetry #8014 \\\"closed\\\" \\\"superseded\\\" \\\"merge\\\" \\\"alternative\\\" context restoration\", \"similarity_threshold\": 0.2, \"vector_weight\": 0.3, \"keyword_search\": false, \"da